      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): turn large pasted text into compact composer attachments",
        "body": "![Composer with image and pasted text attachments](https://calm-mill-vpd8.here.now/pasted-text-with-image.png)\n\n![Composer with pasted text attachment only](https://calm-mill-vpd8.here.now/pasted-text-only.png)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis changes the Control UI composer so plain-text pastes over 1000 characters become compact `text/plain` attachments instead of filling the textarea.\n\nThe attachment uses the existing chat attachment payload path. When the user sends it, the chat request includes the pasted text as a file attachment with `mimeType: \"text/plain\"`; when the user clicks “Show in text field”, the attachment is removed and the full paste is restored into the composer draft as normal message text.\n\nShort text pastes still behave like normal textarea input. Image pastes still use the existing image attachment flow.\n\n## Details\n\n- Converts long plain-text paste events into `pasted-text-*.txt` composer attachments.\n- Shows a compact attachment card with a short preview from the pasted text.\n- Keeps the default composer placeholder for pasted-text-only attachments.\n- Uses the same remove button treatment for image and pasted-text attachments.\n- Preserves the existing attachment send path for retry, queueing, cleanup, and payload serialization.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check ui/src/pages/chat/components/chat-composer.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-send.test.ts ui/src/styles/chat/layout.css`\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- `node_modules/.bin/vitest run ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-send.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.ui.config.ts` (`231` tests passed)\n",
